# Github-Sync Core Decisions

- Keep scope aligned to v1: `GitHub Issues -> Azure DevOps`.
- Use incremental synchronization of new events only.
- Keep the two-stage pipeline: importer stores canonical events, exporter replays to destination.
- Use PostgreSQL + EF Core as the application persistence layer.
- Use Hangfire for recurring jobs and background processing.
- Keep mapping behavior configuration-driven per sync configuration.
- Use exact workflow/status mappings from source to destination.
- Use least-loaded identity mapping for unknown GitHub actors against configured Azure DevOps users.
- Apply skip-and-log for non-blocking record failures.
- Persist failed records in dead-letter storage for replay.
